 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Passive with modal",
     "texto": [
      "It is formed with the conjugated modal + **werden** + participle at the end: **Das muss bezahlt werden** (that has to be paid for). The modal takes second position, and at the end come the two verbs: the participle and **werden**.",
      "With other modals: **Die Ware kann umgetauscht werden** (the goods can be exchanged), **Der Vertrag soll unterschrieben werden** (the contract is to be signed)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Passive in Perfekt",
     "texto": [
      "The process passive in Perfekt is formed with **conjugated sein + Partizip II of the main verb + worden**: **Die Ware ist gestern geliefert worden** (the goods were delivered yesterday). **Worden** appears after the main participle; do not confuse this order with the state passive (**Die Ware ist geliefert**). Here **worden** is the form used in the passive, not the adjectival participle **geworden**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Form",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Meaning",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "modal + werden + participle",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Das muss bezahlt werden.",
